  "content": {
    "id": "p37-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "A multiple choice test has eight questions each with four options. An ill-prepared student adopts the policy of guessing the answer to each of the questions. Suppose that each guess is an independent trial with probability of success $\\frac{1}{4}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p37-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What is the probability that the student will obtain a pass score of at least 50%?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7459}{65536}\\approx0.11$",
          "worked": "Let $X$ be the number of correct answers. Then $X\\sim\\operatorname{Bin}(8,\\frac14)$, and a pass requires at least four correct answers.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X\\ge4)&=\\sum_{k=4}^{8}\\binom{8}{k}\\left(\\frac14\\right)^k\\left(\\frac34\\right)^{8-k}\\\\P(X\\ge4)&=\\frac{5670+1512+252+24+1}{65536}\\\\P(X\\ge4)&=\\frac{7459}{65536}\\\\P(X\\ge4)&\\approx0.11.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "A second test has an even number of questions, each with four options. The probability that a student obtains a pass score by independent guessing is less than 5%. What is the least number of questions on the test?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
